      "message": "Done to take into account some additional spaces including the first two characters (which were previously omitted) U+0418 and U+0020. Was not able to fully verify (since I did not have a russian font and for that reason acrobat showed question marks instead of the actual font).\n\nWhat I instead did to verify this was look at the output pattern. I relied on the fact that U+0418 maps consistently in both Acrobat and PDFium (assuming nothing wrong with either in terms of unicode-\u003etext conversion).\n\nBoth (acrobat and PDFium) generated a spacing pattern as:\n```\nx xxxxx xx xxxxxxxx xxxxxxxxx xxxxxx \\r\\n\nxxxxxxx xxxxxxxxx xxxx xxxxxx x xxxxxx \\r\\n\n... 4 more lines\n```\n\nBoth tools produce identical space/newline placement across all lines. Hence we can deduce that the character count of the edited version matches acrobat. Hence I verified that the 278 from the new version is indeed correct.\n\nLet me know if there is an issue with my logic here, or if I am missing something.\n\nNote: the old pdfium code does not follow the pattern, the first line begins with\n\n`xxxxx xx ...` instead of the expected `x xxxxx xx ...`. In addition some other spaces and characters are removed throughout.\nHence resulting in a lower count of 268 (as it was initially), and hence why 278 is correct.",
